fuxi: 0117 -- the phone resets itself: dead-man timer, and panics reboot

Two failures keep costing a human trip to the phone: the host goes away (or USB
never comes up) and the boot sits there forever, and a panic halts the SoC where
only a hand can reach it.  Both now end in a PSCI reset the device performs alone.

  sweetdeadman=<seconds>   reset when no host command has arrived for that long
                           (default 600).  A conversation keeps it alive; silence
                           ends the boot, so nothing stale outlives the session
                           watching it.  0 disables.
  sweetpanicreset=0        keep halt-on-panic for a hands-on debugging session;
                           default is to flush the ring, then reset, so a crashed
                           phone returns to something the host can reach.

The supervisor starts from fuxi_usb_probe(), not from the gadget, because it has to
cover the case where the gadget never appears.  Timestamps come from mach time, and
the last-command stamp is updated by both command channels.

Limits, stated plainly: neither survives a kernel that stops executing entirely.
That needs a hardware watchdog armed below XNU, and this board's watchdog base is in
neither the ADT nor the sm8550.dtsi I have -- worth finding, but it is not this
patch.

Harness: applied=116 skipped=0.
